# Feature Implementation Guide

This guide explains how to implement a new feature from scratch using our established clean architecture framework, based on the courses feature implementation.

before for we implement any feature we would first check if  we need to write migration from the feature plan, if we need any migration we would add too in  supabase\migrations

we are naming the migrations sequentially (001, 002, 003... nnn). Always check the existing migrations folder to see the latest number and add your new migration to the end of the sequence. For example, if the latest migration is 016_add_delete_policies.sql, then your new migration should be 017_your_migration_name.sql. NEVER edit any existing migration file except if explicitly asked to, only add new ones. Make sure you read all the other relevant migration files to see how we did it and always write RLS policies and make sure you grant access to authenticated users. pls avoid using dart keywords in enums ot any database stuff

After creating i will personally run run the migration files in the Supabase dashboard, the models will be automatically generated. If your migration creates any new database enums, you must add them to the enums section in supadart.yaml before running the generation. Then run `supadart` in the terminal to generate the Dart models from the database schema. This will create/update the model files in the lib/models/ directory based on your new database tables.

## 🚨 CRITICAL: Model Generation Rules

### **Agent Restrictions on Model Creation**
- **ONLY the human can run migrations and generate Dart models**
- **Agents MUST NOT create model files or use generic classes**
- **Agents should code as if models exist, ignoring lint errors**
- **When the human generates models, everything will fall into place**

### **Implementation Pattern**
When implementing a feature that requires new database models:
1. **Agent writes the migration file** (SQL schema)
2. **Agent writes all code** (repositories, blocs, views) **as if models exist**
3. **Agent ignores lint errors** caused by missing models
4. **Human runs migration** in Supabase dashboard
5. **Human runs `supadart`** to generate models
6. **All lint errors resolve automatically** once models are generated

**Example:**
```dart
// ✅ CORRECT: Agent writes code using model as if it exists
import 'package:learn/models/space_assignments.dart'; // Model doesn't exist yet - that's OK

class AssignmentRepository {
  Future<Either<Failure, List<SpaceAssignments>>> getAssignments() async {
    // Code as if SpaceAssignments model exists
    // Lint errors are expected and will resolve after model generation
  }
}
```

```dart
// ❌ WRONG: Agent should NOT create model files
// Don't create lib/models/space_assignments.dart manually
// Don't use generic Map<String, dynamic> as a workaround
``` 


## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

Our features follow **Clean Architecture with MVVM pattern**:

```
lib/features/[feature_name]/
├── di/                     # Dependency Injection
├── data/                   # Data Layer (Repository Implementation)
├── domain/                 # Domain Layer (Repository Interface)
├── presentation/           # Presentation Layer (UI)
│   ├── bloc/              # Main Feature State Management (Bloc + Equatable)
│   │   ├── [feature_name]_bloc.dart
│   │   ├── [feature_name]_event.dart
│   │   └── [feature_name]_state.dart
│   ├── cubit/             # Additional State Management (Sync, etc.)
│   │   ├── [feature_name]_sync_cubit.dart
│   │   └── [feature_name]_sync_state.dart
│   ├── views/             # Screens/Pages
│   │   ├── [feature_name]_list_view.dart
│   │   ├── [feature_name]_detail_view.dart
│   │   ├── add_[feature_name]_view.dart
│   │   └── [feature_name]_sync_panel.dart
│   └── widgets/           # Reusable UI Components
│       ├── [feature_name]_card.dart
│       └── [feature_name]_form.dart
├── services/              # Business Logic Services
│   ├── local_[feature_name]_service.dart    # Hive storage
│   ├── [feature_name]_sync_service.dart     # Cloud operations
│   └── ai_[feature_name]_service.dart       # AI integration (if applicable)
└── utils/                 # Feature-specific utilities
    └── [feature_name]_utils.dart
```

