## 📝 Important Notes

### 🚨 CRITICAL: BLoC Async Operations Pattern
**ALWAYS follow this pattern when using `result.fold()` in BLoC event handlers to prevent emitter assertion errors:**

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT: Always await fold() with async callbacks
final result = await _repository.someOperation();

await result.fold(
  (failure) async {  // ✅ Both callbacks must be async
    emit(state.copyWith(error: failure.message));
  },
  (success) async {  // ✅ Both callbacks must be async
    emit(state.copyWith(data: success));
  },
);
```

```dart
// ❌ WRONG: This will cause BLoC emitter assertion errors
result.fold(
  (failure) {  // ❌ Missing async
    emit(state.copyWith(error: failure.message));
  },
  (success) async {  // ❌ Only one callback is async - creates race condition
    emit(state.copyWith(data: success));
  },
);
```

**Why this happens:**
- The `fold` method doesn't wait for async callbacks to complete
- Async callbacks can continue running after the method finishes
- This creates race conditions where multiple `emit` calls happen simultaneously
- BLoC's emitter prevents concurrent emissions, causing assertion errors

**The fix:**
- Always use `await result.fold()`
- Make both success and failure callbacks `async`
- This ensures all async operations complete before the method finishes

### State Management Architecture
**We use different approaches for different types of classes:**

#### 🔧 Equatable for Blocs:
```dart
// Events and States use Equatable
sealed class [FeatureName]Event extends Equatable {
  const [FeatureName]Event();
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [];
}

class [FeatureName]State extends Equatable {
  const [FeatureName]State({...});
  
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [...];
  
  // Manual copyWith implementation
  [FeatureName]State copyWith({...}) {
    return [FeatureName]State(...);
  }
}
```

#### ❄️ Freezed for Models:
```dart
// Models continue to use Freezed for rich functionality
@freezed
class [ModelName] with _$[ModelName] {
  const factory [ModelName]({
    required String id,
    required String name,
    // ... other fields
  }) = _[ModelName];

  factory [ModelName].fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) =>
      _$[ModelName]FromJson(json);
}
```

### Benefits of This Approach:
✅ **No build_runner for blocs** - Faster development iteration  
✅ **Rich model functionality** - Keep freezed features for data classes  
✅ **Clean separation** - Different tools for different purposes  
✅ **Less complexity** - Simpler bloc implementations  
✅ **Better performance** - No code generation overhead for state management  

### Supabase Syntax Patterns
**ALWAYS use the correct Supabase syntax with supadart-generated models:**

#### ✅ Correct Syntax:
```dart
// Import supadart_header for table accessors
import 'package:learn/models/supadart_header.dart';

// Use table accessors instead of .from()
final data = await _supabase.[table_name]   // ✅ Correct
    .select('*')
    .eq([ModelName].c_id, id)
    .withConverter([ModelName].converter);

// Use model column constants
.eq([ModelName].c_id, id)                   // ✅ Correct
.select([ModelName].c_fieldName)            // ✅ Correct

// Use model update methods
final updateData = [ModelName].update(fieldName: value);
await _supabase.[table_name].update(updateData);  // ✅ Correct

// Use converters properly for single items
final item = [ModelName].converterSingle(itemData);  // ✅ Correct

// For maybeSingle() queries that might return null
final itemData = await _supabase.[table_name]
    .select('*')
    .eq([ModelName].c_id, id)
    .maybeSingle();

if (itemData != null) {
  final item = [ModelName].converterSingle(itemData);
}
```

#### ❌ Incorrect Syntax (Don't use):
```dart
// Don't use .from() with string table names
final data = await _supabase.from('table_name')  // ❌ Wrong

// Don't use hardcoded column names
.eq('id', id)                               // ❌ Wrong
.select('field_name')                       // ❌ Wrong

// Don't use manual JSON objects
await _supabase.from('table_name')          // ❌ Wrong
    .update({'field_name': value});

// Don't use .withConverter() with single converters
.withConverter([ModelName].converterSingle)  // ❌ Wrong (type error)

// Don't use .fromJson() when you have converters
final item = [ModelName].fromJson(itemData);  // ❌ Less preferred
