## 🗄️ **Local Storage with Hive & Sync Panel Architecture**

### **Overview**
Based on the rightal_flashcards implementation, we use an **offline-first approach** with Hive for local storage and a sync panel for managing cloud synchronization. This ensures the app works seamlessly offline while providing sync capabilities when online.

### **Architecture Components**

#### **1. Local Service (Hive Storage)**
```dart
class Local[FeatureName]Service {
  static const String _itemsBoxName = '[feature_name]_box';
  static const String _syncStatusBoxName = '[feature_name]_sync_status_box';
  static const String _syncQueueBoxName = '[feature_name]_sync_queue_box';

  late Box<Map> _itemsBox;
  late Box<Map> _syncStatusBox;
  late Box<Map> _syncQueueBox;

  // Core CRUD operations
  Future<void> save[Item]([ModelName] item) async;
  Future<[ModelName]?> get[Item](String itemId) async;
  Future<List<[ModelName]>> get[Items]ForUser(String userId) async;
  Future<void> delete[Item](String itemId) async;

  // Sync management
  Future<List<Map<String, dynamic>>> getUnsyncedItems() async;
  Future<void> markAsSynced(String itemId) async;
  Future<Map<String, dynamic>?> getSyncStatus(String itemId) async;
}
```

#### **2. Sync Service (Cloud Operations)**
```dart
class [FeatureName]SyncService {
  // Upload operations
  Future<Either<Failure, [ModelName]>> upload[Item]({
    required [ModelName] item,
    String? deviceId,
  }) async;

  // Download operations
  Future<Either<Failure, List<[ModelName]>>> downloadAll[Items]({
    required String userId,
  }) async;

  // Batch operations
  Future<Either<Failure, List<[ModelName]>>> upload[Items]({
    required List<[ModelName]> items,
  }) async;
}
```

#### **3. Sync Cubit (Sync Panel State Management)**
```dart
class [FeatureName]SyncCubit extends Cubit<[FeatureName]SyncState> {
  // Load content from both local and cloud
  Future<void> loadAllContent(String userId) async;
  
